 ## Background
 *   **Origin:** Proposed in the paper "PERF: Panoramic Neural Radiance Field From a Single Panorama" [S1].
-*   **History:** Developed to address the limitations of existing NeRF methods in handling single panorama inputs, specifically the lack of semantic coherence and geometric validity in occluded regions. It builds on Instant-NGP [40] and integrates Stable Diffusion 2 [61] for content completion [S1].
+*   **History:** Developed to address the limitations of existing NeRF methods in handling single panorama inputs, specifically the lack of semantic coherence and geometric validity in occluded regions [S1]. It builds on Instant-NGP [40] and integrates Stable Diffusion 2 [61] for content completion [S1].
 *   **Usage:** Used for single panorama novel view synthesis and extended to applications like text-to-3D and 3D scene stylization [S1]. User studies showed ~81% preference for PERF results over DS-NeRF, SinNeRF, and DietNeRF [S1].
 
